Task: The LogManager handles both formatting and network IO. Split this God Class into two distinct classes obeying the Single Responsibility Principle.

Submitted code:
```
class Formatter {
  format(msg) {
    return `[LOG]: ${msg}`;
  }
}

class Transport {
  send(payload) {
    // In a real app, this might be an API call or file write
    console.log(`Sending data: ${payload}`);
    return true;
  }
}

class App {
  constructor(formatter, transport) {
    this.formatter = formatter;
    this.transport = transport;
  }

  // The "glue" method that makes the components work together
  log(message) {
    const formattedMessage = this.formatter.format(message);
    return this.transport.send(formattedMessage);
  }
}

// --- Usage ---
const myApp = new App(new Formatter(), new Transport());
myApp.log("System initialization complete."); 
// Result: Sending data: [LOG]: System initialization complete.
```

